  <div style='background:#fdfbf7; border:1px solid #e2d9cc; border-left:4px solid #064e3b; padding:15px; border-radius:6px; margin-bottom:14px;'>
    <h2 style='color:#064e3b; font-size:14px; margin:0 0 8px 0; font-weight:800; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:1px;'>THE WEEKLY FINAL • WEEK 6 👑</h2>
    <div style='color:#334155; font-size:12px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;'>
      <p style='margin: 0 0 10px 0; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 12px; color: #334155;'>The final whistle of Monday Night Football has echoed across Levi&rsquo;s Stadium, and Week 6 is officially sealed in the Branham Hills vault! In a primetime showdown for the Faithful, the <strong>San Francisco 49ers</strong> defeated the <strong>Washington Commanders 23&ndash;17</strong> (Combined MNF Total: 40 points) to remain unbeaten at 6&ndash;0. Across an upset-heavy 14-game Week 6 slate where Denver stunned Seattle (17&ndash;14), Cleveland edged Baltimore (13&ndash;10), Tennessee toppled Indianapolis (26&ndash;20), Carolina upset Philadelphia (25&ndash;14), and Arizona shocked the Rams (18&ndash;16), surviving Sunday required nerves of steel.</p>
      <p style='margin: 0 0 10px 0; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 12px; color: #334155;'>Standing tall at the summit and capturing the prestigious <strong>Week 6 Crown outright is Jessica</strong>, who navigated the minefield with a slate-leading <strong>9 outright victories (9&ndash;5, TB: 51)</strong>! Entering Monday Night with a solo 8&ndash;5 lead over chasers Don (7&ndash;6) and Brian (7&ndash;6)—after only Jessica, Don, and Brian had the vision to punch Denver&rsquo;s Thursday night ticket—all 12 contenders across the entire Branham Hills league locked in the <strong>San Francisco 49ers</strong> on Monday Night Football! When the 49ers closed out Washington 23&ndash;17, every contender notched a Monday night victory and Jessica sealed her wire-to-wire solo Week 6 championship!</p>
      <p style='margin: 0 0 10px 0; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 12px; color: #334155;'>Right on the champion&rsquo;s heels, <strong>Don (8&ndash;6, TB: 55)</strong> and <strong>Brian (8&ndash;6, TB: 149)</strong> shared Co-Runner-Up honors on the silver step of the podium. Behind them, a massive six-contender pack deadlocked at <strong>7&ndash;7</strong> (<strong>Rudy, Tyler, Elvis, Jennifer, Jordan, and Trevor</strong>), while <strong>Lanny</strong> and <strong>Marcio</strong> finished at <strong>6&ndash;8</strong>. In the overall season race through 6 weeks, <strong>Rudy (59 wins)</strong> holds a 1-point edge over <strong>Lanny (58 wins)</strong>, with newly crowned Week 6 Champion <strong>Jessica (57 wins)</strong> charging into solo 3rd place just two games off the lead!</p>
      <p style='margin: 0 0 10px 0; line-height: 1.6; font-size: 12px; color: #334155;'>Down at the damp bottom of the Week 6 sheet, your humble Admin <strong>Joel (5&ndash;9, TB: 58)</strong> officially draws solo cellar cleanup duty after backing the wrong side of Sunday&rsquo;s coin-flip upsets. As Don &ldquo;The Commish&rdquo; Threet always put it: <em>&ldquo;Winners Walk, Losers Stalk!&rdquo;</em> One Penalty Flag goes straight into The Umpire Penalty Jar, the chalkboard is wiped clean at midnight, and Week 7 pick sheets are now open for Tuesday morning submissions!</p>
    </div>
  </div>

